From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 16:59:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] proof: P0-7 public API survives a Clerk misconfiguration, and
 readiness names it

- app.ts: clerkMiddleware wrapped so a configuration failure yields no auth
  context instead of a 500. Public routes are anonymous by definition
- authGuard: all five getAuth callers guarded. requireAuth / requireAdminRole /
  requireDealerRole answer 401 instead of 500; optionalAuth continues; requireDbUser
  falls back safely. Still fails closed - no protected route serves data
- health.ts: clerk_config appears in readyz checks but does NOT flip readiness.
  A 503 would take a working public site out of rotation because sign-in is broken
- test helper deletes detached lead_history before hard-deleting a user, because
  Gate 4 makes that row survive its listing. Production never hard-deletes a user
- full API suite: 511 passed, 3 skipped, 0 failed
